meta {
  name: negative create wrong enrollmentId type
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url_integration_api}}/api/v1/auth-attempts
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{integrationKey}}
  password: {{secretKey}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/problem+json
}

body:json {
  {
      "enrollmentId": "not-an-integer",
      "challengeRequested": false
  }
}

script:post-response {
  test("Status is 4xx (schema or request validation)", function () {
      expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.at.least(400);
      expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.below(500);
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  Deliberately invalid Integration create body: `enrollmentId` is a string, but the OpenAPI
  schema requires `integer` (`int32`). A well-formed SDK or Demo App client cannot produce this
  request. `challengeRequested` stays a valid boolean so the type mismatch is the probe.

  Cloudflare validates request shape only (method, path, JSON body). It does not check API-key
  validity, IP whitelist, or enrollment ownership. Dummy Basic credentials are enough for the
  edge check.

  **Use with environment `exp1`.** `base_url_integration_api` is
  `https://exp1-integration-api.ezkey.org`.

  On EXP1 Cloudflare schema validation **Block**, expect HTTP **403** Error **1020** (API Shield
  / WAF). Bruno sends `Accept` JSON / problem+json, so the body is Cloudflare's RFC 9457 JSON
  (`cloudflare_error: true`, `error_code: 1020`, `ray_id`, `type` under
  `developers.cloudflare.com`), not an Ezkey `https://ezkey.io/problems/…` ProblemDetail.

  A Spring ProblemDetail (`type` under `https://ezkey.io/problems/`, often HTTP 400 or 401)
  means the request **reached origin** — not schema-Block evidence. That is the expected
  outcome when Set action is **None** (product default). Against **local**, Jackson/Bean
  Validation also returns 4xx; that is not a Cloudflare check.

  **Do not add this request to `bruno-health.sh` suites.** Operator reading:
  `docs/cloudflare/integration-api-schema-validation.md` § Reading responses.
}
